Provenance
----------
This package holds the real-time analytics of TraderX (product name
"QuantRiskPro V2.0"), a trading-management system prototype the author wrote
alone in 2025-2026. The work was prompted by a remote freelance enquiry that
was never concluded: no contract was signed, no payment was made and nothing
was delivered or accepted, so no rights were transferred. The TraderX
repository stays private because it also holds the enquirer's requirement
documents and data files; none of that material is included here.

The code was copied from TraderX backend-python at revision 156d265e on
2026-11-12, into a fresh git history: src/engine/realtime, src/engine/models
(without signal_providers.py), src/engine/online_learning, src/datasources,
src/exchanges, src/observability and src/core/mock_guard.py, plus the tests
that exercise them. The exact list of what was taken, left out and changed is
in docs/PROVENANCE.md. Two sibling packages were extracted earlier from the
same host: quantrisk-core (indicators, strategies, backtesting) and
agent-runtime-kit (the agent runtime).

Some source files keep the headers they had in TraderX ("Copyright 2025
TraderX. All rights reserved." / "SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0");
most have none. "TraderX" is a name the author used for that project. All
files in this repository, with or without a header, are distributed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

Not verified: whether the TraderX code itself contains fragments from other
sources; it was not traced file by file.

Third-party software
--------------------
No third-party source code is bundled. Dependencies (numpy, pandas, scipy,
aiohttp, fastapi; optional websockets, redis, prometheus_client,
opentelemetry, scikit-learn, xgboost, torch, arch, statsmodels, akshare,
ccxt, aiosmtplib) are installed separately under their own licenses. The
exchange and data-source adapters only call public APIs; using them is
subject to each provider's terms.
